" :answer-field/key "$(2,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed83a8d6-9e07-5905-be1f-34b393c3d6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439929} {:answer/id #uuid "dcef0c5c-1acb-5551-97b3-3f576bf135b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439930}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439929} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e3dbaf6-9358-5c2a-9801-aef6c67ddc06" :answer-field/key "$(2,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440322} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065e1081-b5f1-5f33-a472-b91a349b1ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439931} {:answer/id #uuid "4bed7d93-95ff-5f0a-9e8a-462b709673d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439932}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439932} :answer-field/id #uuid "a537d884-e552-57b7-b8f8-e2de9abb83a0" :answer-field/key "$(2,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9c0801c9-8ff6-5c1f-a200-5a0877707694" :question/math-academy-id "q-72410" :question/problem "At which points on the curve ${y}^{2}+2xy={x}^{2}+8$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2xy & ={x}^{2}+8 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=8.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2})i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2})j \\\\  & =2(y+x)\\,i-2(y-x)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ (2(y+x)\\,i-2(y-x)\\,j)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ -2(y-x) & =0 \\\\ y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=x$ into the equation of our curve gives:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ (x)^{2}+2x(x)-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $x=2$, we get $y=2$ and the corresponding point is $(2,2).$\n\n- If $x=-2$, we get $y=-2$ and the corresponding point is $(-2,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "913ad9eb-89eb-5a60-ac19-fc37d153f23a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439933} {:answer/id #uuid "38454e86-b9b2-5147-b5f5-57a1c469fc1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439934}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439933} :answer-field/id #uuid "913b33c0-9682-5034-a4bc-ca4b66f58927" :answer-field/key "$(-4,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440324} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b48cb1-a3d5-5e03-bba7-fd3e349f22a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439935} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef79959-5b46-5fd5-a1f2-b3ef81d41dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439936}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439936} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b08edc5-487a-5110-8658-6a853845ba9c" :answer-field/key "$(-4,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dbbf91c-fcf7-5749-8e10-99b79b6c2f27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439937} {:answer/id #uuid "94fb39d0-64da-5f0a-b3b3-e2111e0d9543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439938}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439937} :answer-field/id #uuid "8398fd52-93e4-5dbf-a834-63438c1d40be" :answer-field/key "$(-2,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97953d8e-c87c-5d26-9a7f-f79a3f0d99df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439939} {:answer/id #uuid "a551023e-5f0c-51b5-bac1-843707e77a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439940}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439940} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbad587e-fa9a-560c-98d8-d474ad89b641" :answer-field/key "$(-1,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440327} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93414178-3753-5420-b4b6-1ac48e45c3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439941} {:answer/id #uuid "a6414388-a002-593f-a04a-4268450d1c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439942}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439941} :answer-field/id #uuid "c37025ed-9888-5ac7-953f-6d2173c4ec86" :answer-field/key "$(-1,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440328} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0e94f97-83d4-55d1-a4fe-2eecc3c33c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439943} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b286d5-0094-5d27-8122-cf59c572339d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439944}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439943} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a071a57-c0a2-5ff5-8488-5bd97002af7b" :answer-field/key "$(1,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7f8d1ef-4d2a-52c3-97a7-ce498c4ce11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439945} {:answer/id #uuid "35e5554f-349d-51bb-9ccd-94b46e947c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439946}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439945} :answer-field/id #uuid "d02f2705-c6d5-5710-8589-44dd2b88e45c" :answer-field/key "$(4,-4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5577e429-0d55-5dd4-b588-49ac727edd6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72440" :question/problem "At which points on the curve ${x}^{2}+2xy=-5y+4$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2xy & =-5y+4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2xy+5y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2xy+5y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=4.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+2xy+5y)i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+2xy+5y)j \\\\  & =(2x+5)\\,i-(2x+2y)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ ((2x+5)\\,i-(2x+2y)\\,j)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ -(2x+2y) & =0 \\\\ x & =-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-y$ into the equation of our curve gives:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2xy+5y & =4 \\\\ (-y)^{2}+2(-y)y+5y & =4 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+5y & =4 \\\\ -{y}^{2}+5y-4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-5y+4 & =0 \\\\ (y-1)(y-4) & =0 \\\\ y & =1\\,\\text{or}\\,y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $y=1$, we get $x=-1$ and the corresponding point is $(-1,1).$\n\n- If $y=4$, we get $x=-4$ and the corresponding point is $(-4,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a24f4b8-a184-5828-8c72-dcc5b94e5943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\,i-5\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336423} {:answer/id #uuid "2afed586-1f6a-50fd-ad21-c54f17e514f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336436} {:answer/id #uuid "af297190-71a7-5741-8317-95edf63e83e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "i+5\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337604} {:answer/id #uuid "be71b2b4-857d-5122-ac95-bc07fb632330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\,i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337725} {:answer/id #uuid "c71d302c-3c74-5be4-b48a-d3f52171a59d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337799}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337799} :answer-field/id #uuid "26dc6ba3-c35c-5f43-8491-310a9b2258ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3c4a11cf-62cb-5e11-869c-4992e2a1b6f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-72463" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-4xy=1-3x.$ Find a tangent vector to that curve at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-4xy & =1-3x \\\\ 2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-4xy+3x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-4xy+3x$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(1,1)$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(1,1)={f}_{y}(1,1)i-{f}_{x}(1,1)j\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-4xy+3x)i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-4xy+3x)j \\\\  & =(4y{x}^{3}-4x)i-(6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4y+3)j \\\\ t(1,1) & =(4(1)(1)^{3}-4(1))i-(6(1)^{2}(1)^{2}-4(1)+3)j \\\\  & =-5\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our tangent vector is $-5\\,j.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a99ac4-61b4-5a56-b3ac-d93de9f9dd89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339144} {:answer/id #uuid "4904f1fc-dc77-524c-af2d-813ee70dcc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339783} {:answer/id #uuid "a8efa69b-78be-5a02-81b6-baa9e8fedd59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340664} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd060fa-0631-5438-80c1-f6c14e340129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340956} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c989e2-03ee-581f-83f6-e95b613b2103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341033}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339783} :answer-field/id #uuid "013f1fb3-558e-5ad1-b4b7-34a42443c53c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "65bcf244-fd2b-540c-b6fb-6b4c12786b6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73619" :question/problem "![](images/86/8637901efc126236b190e7012cf65a06be078cb21c3093eff39b927493000138.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1.5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "264c8e91-4c93-5aee-ba55-bd907c4a3b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339459} {:answer/id #uuid "320f7703-8c4f-5dc9-8624-856e513ecd8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339568} {:answer/id #uuid "60bbf1c4-341f-50ef-8931-5d66a4141ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339990} {:answer/id #uuid "ba485f5d-a19d-569b-ac5d-342a12dfefea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340797} {:answer/id #uuid "e1dcb36b-eef4-548f-8678-715a402e7c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{32}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341129}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340797} :answer-field/id #uuid "d755d6a9-5867-59b0-abe9-3aa060579222" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "72c0e5d1-5884-5875-91c7-7d9b69f20798" :question/math-academy-id "q-73627" :question/problem "![](images/37/377a871e9328e0a8b3c12d8904ecc16a2e6e3a17fa7dba05925bb6f2e5d7e4ad.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c9bf20-8128-53fc-aa86-1964b815386d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339304} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb7e5b-2acb-5ebe-ad55-584b08e3b9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} {:answer/id #uuid "534af3da-95e9-55b2-aba8-6f4b454b8ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339896} {:answer/id #uuid "90dc551e-639b-50fc-9023-134528ddbdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340425} {:answer/id #uuid "c5917a7f-b9e8-5505-bca8-86a9c397ec2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340880}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} :answer-field/id #uuid "64dee0d1-0120-5112-8fc9-ab060cbba4c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6203036f-b82a-557b-b713-2351ced43cc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-74087" :question/problem "Calculate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d4e53ff-430e-5b10-b738-cd8dd3d0256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339385} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9151d3-7fde-540f-b82e-0580c7384593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339807} {:answer/id #uuid "989f6c04-735e-50e5-8fdd-bb014b8275b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340506} {:answer/id #uuid "add28c3c-0b54-53af-97fb-51c4b2116412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} {:answer/id #uuid "f90418c6-311c-5a49-b4cf-0366851ed196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{6}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} :answer-field/id #uuid "0614f8dc-7023-5386-a910-5a8612abf41b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b94b38f3-a670-562e-93ec-c45c6d3b0d77" :question/math-academy-id "q-74088" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e99b757-9d06-5cfc-8db6-a2492878332c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{10}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339262} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4fd180-d811-5662-8d7f-8cf39e6abded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339651} {:answer/id #uuid "73d61482-1a92-5fde-a598-f549899e13ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f2d102-e8a3-564e-981d-58e57522a465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340754} {:answer/id #uuid "da9ff3c8-cb06-5827-af7c-d34ff6bef005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341070}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a2565c-7c88-5b3a-b2f9-3d057c775bea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "31ac68e1-bc05-5634-b712-63c327f4e3c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74090" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=10x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=10 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 10x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa3632a-36d9-5d45-aada-3fed83e6dce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342326} {:answer/id #uuid "653b4691-0f44-5149-acb3-ba490ce5be44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343095} {:answer/id #uuid "beffe86d-8d35-5522-bff5-c1bacb25479e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343916} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4cf03e-744a-54e5-90b3-81ce5dcd317d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344026} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9286e2-fe14-5bfe-9359-f7ac47372d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344051}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342326} :answer-field/id #uuid "445577e8-8f70-5d8d-a39d-41e0418a56ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a32523f7-b65a-5ea6-ad9b-ea76193dc862" :question/math-academy-id "q-74909" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,2)}\\operatorname{ln}(4-x-y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-x-y).\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous except when $4-x-y$  is negative or zero. However, at the point $(1,2)$,  the expression  $4-x-y$ is positive, so we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(1,2)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,2)}\\operatorname{ln}(4-x-y) &=\\operatorname{ln}(4-1-2)=\\operatorname{ln}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52b7df89-d99c-5b42-9cc2-063604231fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342929} {:answer/id #uuid "8e43633a-b13b-5b08-9991-4a855a976614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343484} {:answer/id #uuid "be0eb3e2-b2bb-5b4d-8e0b-d09e4ab2c128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343913} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8ebb93-6c86-56d6-af46-1bb108780271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344050} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a1e3df-1ed6-57d4-81e0-257ba2a81c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342929} :answer-field/id #uuid "a81e50a8-3dec-549b-a0cf-3a09d9dfb58b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3f277d23-3dcb-54b8-9f1f-cefa2a015d92" :question/math-academy-id "q-74912" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{xy}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous for all values of $x$ and $y.$ So,  we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(-2,4)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy} &=\\sqrt{(-2)\\cdot 4}=\\sqrt[3]{-8}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "154cde04-acab-5465-9547-10829d1c2ac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342426} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb42284-ebac-5722-a55a-f3d61f6c5806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343155} {:answer/id #uuid "92dfc28e-190d-569d-937c-6a93104fd226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343523} {:answer/id #uuid "b4342938-2831-524c-937b-68dbdb102e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343816} {:answer/id #uuid "dcaa824e-6288-5d0e-ba41-9737c9cd645c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344174}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342426} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e203f08-9966-5d66-bfae-16443836045d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "267b24cc-56d4-5780-90e2-1ea13cc5ba4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74918" :question/problem "Find  $\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz}.$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz}=\\frac{1\\cdot {2}^{2}-1\\cdot {2}^{2}}{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz} & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{(x-y){z}^{2}}{(y-x)z} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1,2)}-\\frac{(x-y){z}^{2}}{(x-y)z} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1,2)}(-z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1,2)}(-z) & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e684a3-31e7-5afb-abe6-889eedabcb7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342537} {:answer/id #uuid "428a1d63-be06-5a77-98e9-2febf282827f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342789} {:answer/id #uuid "49075012-2ea9-548d-9ca7-add606c5a0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342838} {:answer/id #uuid "6d62d708-9b60-5aa8-8bc8-d437253c8433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343176} {:answer/id #uuid "9a659bec-94b4-5e6e-bfad-430d6af2dd3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343597}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343176} :answer-field/id #uuid "68b1ada5-9d1d-5909-9bba-0575aa292e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "985d9983-0c2e-5408-a2e7-d78f48fa4c2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-74952" :question/problem "Find  $\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}=\\frac{(-1)^{2}+2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1+{1}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{(x+y)^{2}}{(y-x)(y+x)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{(x+y)(x+y)}{(y-x)(x+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{x+y}{y-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{x+y}{y-x} & =\\frac{(-1)+1}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a374dad-4f6b-524a-aa54-86b138bf78f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342993} {:answer/id #uuid "63a029bd-31fb-55ab-850e-9758cb89df9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343081} {:answer/id #uuid "8849f804-0c8c-53f5-8a8d-500546d52a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343419} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9051dc-e91b-5b6b-8909-a2310cbbc28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343442} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9e25dd-2c46-5b76-99a3-260d2e1e558e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343081} :answer-field/id #uuid "b313de74-d195-5d45-bc88-f2346a3b2f91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "774103b5-b3b5-52ef-9d71-0bba2999450c" :question/math-academy-id "q-74957" :question/problem "$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2}}{x-y-2}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2}}{x-y-2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{1+2}}{3-1-2}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2}}{x-y-2} & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})}{(x-y-2)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-(\\sqrt{y+2})^{2}}{(x-y-2)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{x-y-2}{(x-y-2)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (3,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2}} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{1+2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24eddf01-84ca-55d1-a380-e9e3dc0ff46c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342549} {:answer/id #uuid "46dbb611-211c-5a6d-87c1-e6d11b78516f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342824} {:answer/id #uuid "5b00ef31-06ca-5784-b242-7ba648259786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342998} {:answer/id #uuid "5f565846-c8fc-53fd-9002-a2c55e2b4a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343042} {:answer/id #uuid "740303a6-c0b7-5dc3-b4d8-e1c846a9c24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343243}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343042} :answer-field/id #uuid "e02b8a03-215d-5182-84e4-5ebedc1e9c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "324536b7-fcd9-5a5e-87fe-4723a8ba3a5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74958" :question/problem "$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-y}{x-{y}^{2}}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-y}{x-{y}^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1}-1}{1-{1}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-y}{x-{y}^{2}} & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-y)(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-{y}^{2}}{(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{x-{y}^{2}}{(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5225a54e-55a7-5758-ada6-d6e76ec121f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342920} {:answer/id #uuid "6afe5058-ed29-5490-84ca-cf5ea037f221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343150} {:answer/id #uuid "72810408-6a46-5e8d-9beb-52bbe2e8f436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343231} {:answer/id #uuid "c186d6e7-0ac4-5259-897c-07e60f6cc561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343939} {:answer/id #uuid "fd70e6c7-52f3-50c1-9a16-a6b4b41da448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344465}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343150} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5121edc-c04d-5ea2-9e7a-1a1ca983765e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "580ed3de-301a-5585-aa08-af0b5b637cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-74960" :question/problem "$\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{\\sqrt{x}-y}=$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{\\sqrt{x}-y}=\\frac{{1}^{2}-1}{\\sqrt{1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{\\sqrt{x}-y} & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{({y}^{2}-x)(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{(\\sqrt{x}-y)(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{({y}^{2}-x)(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}\\frac{-(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{x-{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}-(\\sqrt{x}+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (1,1)}-(\\sqrt{x}+y) & =-(\\sqrt{1}+1) \\\\  & =-(1+1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345004 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f3e9a8-09a1-5f57-86fa-04e7b6915e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468094} {:answer/id #uuid "78fcd3c1-4a11-58fd-8ce6-df88fc49f25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468095}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468095} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6cf87b-5ae8-56c1-a044-0835a6c8cde4" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311f4a3b-6073-5441-be15-0e0c7cc774ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468096} {:answer/id #uuid "88d6ad28-2d86-517c-95bc-f86d6c74568c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468097}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468097} :answer-field/id #uuid "d491b47c-a016-53fb-a14f-bea3b0d37235" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5f46b92-20fa-5e06-82d5-4d57f3b2567e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468098} {:answer/id #uuid "5c70d63f-3608-5e38-a9a1-5aca4eef4730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468099}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468098} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0d14fb0-548c-5014-9418-0de578d5c27b" :answer-field/key "The limit exists and is equal to $2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d5fe00a2-ab56-5281-b3c2-6fe8dad2417a" :question/math-academy-id "q-74964" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\frac{2\\cdot {0}^{2}}{2\\cdot {0}^{2}-0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$” is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{x(2x-1)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{2x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{2\\cdot 0-1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$” is also true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit exists and is equal to $2$” is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}]}
